        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Ephrem the Syrian</strong> <em>Commentary on Genesis</em> <small>(c. 360 AD)</small><p>Ephrem reads &#x27;In the beginning&#x27; as denoting the absolute commencement of created time, not a moment within a prior temporal sequence. The Word through whom God creates is not added to creation but is its enabling cause; thus the verse is read Christologically without dissolving the Father-Son distinction. Ethiopian Tewahedo commentary follows Ephrem on this point against any reading that would make the Son a creature.</p></aside>',
