        '<strong>NT echoes of Genesis 1:1.</strong> Three foundational New Testament passages consciously rewrite this opening: <a href="index_split_054.html#ch-b63-c1">John 1:1–3</a> ("In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with God, and the Word was God… all things were made through him") identifies the Logos as the divine agent of creation; <a href="index_split_058.html#ch-b71-c1">Colossians 1:16–17</a> identifies that Logos as Christ ("by him all things were created… in him all things hold together"); and <a href="index_split_059.html#ch-b78-c11">Hebrews 11:3</a> reads Genesis 1 as foundational for faith ("by faith we understand that the universe was created by the word of God"). The repeated "and God said" of Genesis 1 is theologically reinterpreted as speech-acts of the pre-incarnate Word.',
