        "Note",
        "<strong>Neshamah (<em>נְשָׁמָה</em>) vs. ruach.</strong> Two distinct “breath/spirit” words appear in Genesis 2: <em>neshamat ḥayyim</em> here (“breath of life,” LXX <em>pnoēn zōēs</em>), and <em>ruḥ</em> elsewhere. Rabbinic tradition (Genesis Rabbah 14:9) lists five distinct soul-words and reads <em>neshamah</em> as the highest. Note that the same breath enters all living creatures in 7:22 — it is not unique to humans, though humans alone receive it from God’s mouth directly.",
        "User paraphrase; references LXX, Genesis Rabbah",
