        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>‘Knowledge of good and evil’ — what is it?</strong> Mainstream readings: (1) moral consciousness — discerning right from wrong; (2) sexual maturity — the phrase used elsewhere of coming of age (Deut 1:39); (3) total knowledge as a Hebrew merism (‘everything from A to Z’); (4) autonomous moral judgment, claiming a divine prerogative. Most modern scholars favor #4.",
