        "He will bruise your head",
        "parallel",
        "Parallel",
        "Parallel: Rom 16:20 / Heb 2:14 / Rev 12 — the protoevangelium",
        '<strong>The "first gospel" (<em>protevangelium</em>).</strong> Patristic and Ethiopian Tewahedo tradition has long read Genesis 3:15 as the first messianic promise: the seed of the woman crushing the serpent\'s head prefigures Christ defeating Satan. New Testament echoes: <a href="index_split_056.html#ch-b65-c16">Romans 16:20</a> ("the God of peace will soon crush Satan under your feet"); <a href="index_split_059.html#ch-b78-c2">Hebrews 2:14</a> ("through death he might destroy the one who has the power of death, that is, the devil"); the entire war of <a href="index_split_060.html#ch-b86-c12">Revelation 12</a>, where the dragon pursues the woman and her seed. The Septuagint\'s use of masculine pronoun (<em>autos</em> "he") rather than expected neuter shaped Christological reading.',
