        "I have gotten a  man with Yahweh’s help",
        "comm-rabbinic",
        "Note",
        "Eve’s first words after the fall",
        '<strong>The first words of human birth.</strong> Eve\'s exclamation at Cain\'s birth plays on his name: <em>qayin</em> ("Cain") echoes <em>qaniti</em> ("I have gotten / acquired / produced"). Some readers (Targum Pseudo-Jonathan, Luther) heard a misplaced messianic hope — Eve thinking Cain might be the promised seed of 3:15. The narrative irony is heavy: this first child becomes the first murderer.',
