        "sin crouches at the door",
        "word",
        "Hebrew",
        "Hebrew",
        "<strong>The grammar of Genesis 4:7 is famously obscure.</strong> A literal rendering: ‘If you do well, [there will be] lifting up. If you do not do well, sin [is] crouching at the door, and to you [is] its desire, and you shall rule over it.’ The Hebrew is so terse that translators must supply much. Note the deliberate echo of Genesis 3:16 (‘your desire shall be for your husband’).",
