        "Note",
        "<strong>One of the most famous rhetorical questions in literature.</strong> <em>Shomer achi</em> — ‘keeper of my brother.’ The verb <em>shamar</em> (to keep, guard) was used in Gen 2:15 of Adam’s task in the garden: he was to <em>shamar</em> it. Cain’s denial of the keeper-relation echoes the broken relation between humanity and the rest of creation.",
