        "<strong>D’mei achikha — ‘your brother’s blood’.</strong> Notably, ‘blood’ here is plural in Hebrew (<em>damim</em>) — ‘bloods.’ Rabbinic tradition (Mishnah Sanhedrin 4:5) interprets this plural as including not only Abel’s blood but the blood of his potential descendants — the basis for the rabbinic principle that to destroy one life is to destroy a whole world.",
