        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>Lamech’s song — the first poetry in the Bible.</strong> The lines display formal Hebrew parallelism (“Adah and Zillah, hear my voice / wives of Lamech, listen to my speech”), the first preserved poetic composition in the canon. Lamech’s claim of seventy-sevenfold vengeance is inverted by Jesus in Matthew 18:22 (“seventy times seven”) into a measure of forgiveness. Rabbinic legend (Tanḥuma Berešit 11) imagines Lamech accidentally killing Cain in the dark, mistaking him for an animal — an attempt to harmonize the violent boast with God’s sevenfold protection of Cain in v.15.",
        "User original",
