        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>Enoch’s ‘translation.’</strong> The Hebrew <em>laqach</em> (took) is the same verb used of Elijah’s ascension in 2 Kings 2:10. Enoch’s departure-without-death is the seed of the entire Enochic tradition (1 Enoch, 2 Enoch, 3 Enoch). The number 365 for his lifespan is widely read as solar-symbolic and forms the basis of the 364-day calendar tradition preserved in 1 Enoch and at Qumran.",
