        "Methuselah’s name and the flood",
        '<strong>Methuselah\'s name as prophecy.</strong> <em>Metushelach</em> may mean "his death will bring" or "man of the spear." In the chronology of Genesis 5–7, Methuselah dies in the year of the flood — the flood comes the year of his death. Rabbinic tradition (Genesis Rabbah 32) and patristic readings alike heard in the name a prophecy of judgment delayed: the longest-lived human in the Bible was a stay of execution upon a doomed world. His grandfather Enoch named him; the name testifies that Enoch already foresaw judgment.',
