        "filled with violence",
        "word",
        "Hebrew",
        "chamas — violence as covenant breach",
        "<strong><em>Chamas</em> (חָמָס) — violence.</strong> The word repeated in 6:11 and 6:13 is the same root that gives the prophetic indictment a name (Jer 6:7; Ezek 7:11; 8:17; Amos 3:10; Hab 1:2–3). It denotes not merely physical violence but lawless aggression — a structural breakdown of justice. Rabbinic tradition (<em>Bereshit Rabbah</em> 31:5) and Targum Onkelos read it as “robbery” — the violation of property rights. The flood, in this reading, is brought not by idolatry but by social collapse: the earth is destroyed when humanity becomes systemically violent.",
        "User paraphrase; references Targum",
