        "b",
        "",
        "word",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>‘The windows of the sky’ — <em>arubot ha-shamayim</em>.</strong> The phrase reflects the Ancient Near Eastern cosmology where the sky was a solid dome (the <em>raqia</em>, ‘firmament’) holding back upper waters. Rain came through windows in this dome. Genesis 1:7 establishes this cosmology; Genesis 7:11 has those windows opened, returning the world to pre-creation watery chaos.",
        "User original",
