        "comm-rabbinic",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>The olive leaf and the dove.</strong> The first sign of the receding flood becomes a layered symbol: peace (Roman tradition), covenant fidelity, the Spirit (cf. Matt 3:16). In the Talmud (b. Eruvin 18b) the dove’s preference for a bitter olive leaf over Noah’s sweet provisions is read as a parable: it is better to receive bitter sustenance from God than sweet sustenance from human hands. Olive cultivation marks the establishment of settled Mediterranean agriculture; the symbol implicitly announces the agricultural-civilizational restart.",
        "User paraphrase; references Talmud",
