        1,
        "",
        "Be fruitful, multiply, and replenish the earth",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>Noahide blessing.</strong> The original creation blessing (1:28) is reissued to Noah’s family. The repetition is significant: post-flood humanity is granted a new beginning with the same mandate. But the blessing is now twinned with a different relationship to the animal world — fear and dread (9:2) — and explicit permission to eat meat (9:3). Eden’s vegetarian order has given way. The Noahide reissuance suggests humanity now operates under modified terms: the original mandate persists, but the conditions of creation have shifted permanently.",
        "User original",
