        "",
        "The sons of Ham were: Cush, Mizraim, Put, and Canaan",
        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Note",
        "Hamitic peoples — Africa and the Levant",
        '<strong>Hamitic peoples.</strong> The four sons of Ham represent the southern arc: <em>Cush</em> = Nubia / Upper Egypt and northern Sudan (modern Ethiopia and Sudan; the same name applies in <a href="index_split_015.html#ch-b11-c19">2 Kings 19:9</a> and <a href="index_split_055.html#ch-b64-c8">Acts 8:27</a> for the Ethiopian eunuch); <em>Mizraim</em> = Egypt (the standard Hebrew name); <em>Put</em> = Libya (or possibly Punt, on the Red Sea); <em>Canaan</em> = the Levant. The grouping reflects geography rather than linguistics — Egyptian and Cushitic are Afro-Asiatic, but Canaanite is Semitic, suggesting the table organizes peoples by political/cultural orbit rather than language family. The Ethiopian Tewahedo tradition reads Cush prominently, claiming descent from this line.',
        "User original",
