        "Parallel",
        "Acts 17:26 — “from one [man]”",
        '<strong>“From one he made every nation.”</strong> <a href="index_split_055.html#ch-b64-c17">Acts 17:26</a> takes the table of nations as the foundation for Paul’s Areopagus argument: “He made from one [man / blood / origin] every nation of mankind to dwell on all the face of the earth, having determined their appointed seasons and the bounds of their habitation.” Genesis 10’s diversity-from-unity becomes the theological premise of universal human kinship and divine providence over national history. <a href="index_split_015.html#ch-b12-c1">1 Chronicles 1:5–23</a> retells the Genesis 10 list almost verbatim, anchoring later Israelite genealogy in the universal-humanity register.',
