        "lit-chiasm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>Literary structure: Babel chiasm.</strong> Gen 11:1-9 forms a tight chiasm centered on YHWH's descent: A (one language, v.1) — B (settle in plain, v.2) — C (build city/tower, vv.3-4) — D (YHWH came down, v.5) — C' (city/tower stalled, vv.6-7) — B' (scattered, v.8) — A' (languages confused, v.9). The reversal at the center is the theological point: human ascent meets divine descent.",
