        "comm-modern-critical",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>Shēm — “a name for ourselves.”</strong> The Hebrew word <em>shēm</em> (name, fame, monument) is the same as the proper name <em>Shem</em>; the builders refuse the divine commission to fill the earth (9:1) and try to make their own <em>shem</em>. Brueggemann reads this as Genesis’s first anti-imperial polemic: the unified <em>technology</em> + <em>language</em> + <em>concentration</em> of Babel is the prototype of every subsequent empire. God’s response — dispersion — is therefore not punishment but corrective: a re-launching of the human project according to its original mandate.",
