        "<strong>Genesis 11 — LXX vs. MT genealogy.</strong> The Septuagint (followed by the Ethiopian canon) and the Masoretic Text differ significantly here. In the LXX, post-Flood patriarchs father children at later ages, adding centuries to the chronology. The LXX also includes a generation absent from the MT: Cainan son of Arpachshad (named in Luke 3:36). This LXX-only Cainan appears in this Bible but is missing from most Protestant Bibles.",
        "User paraphrase; references LXX, Septuagint",
