        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        '<strong>The universal scope of Abraham’s call.</strong> The Abrahamic covenant moves from the particular ("a great nation") to the universal ("all the families"). Paul cites this verse in Galatians 3:8 as "the gospel preached beforehand to Abraham" — the basis for the inclusion of Gentiles in the people of God. The verb is reflexive (<em>nivr’khu</em>) — the nations bless themselves <em>through</em> Abraham, or are blessed in him.',
        "User original",
