        "",
        "seventy-five years old",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>Abraham’s age.</strong> Abraham receives the call at 75. The detail is theologically significant: he is past normal child-bearing prime (his son will not be born for another 25 years), making the promise of nationhood humanly impossible. Hebrews 11:11 will use this to model faith’s “hoping against hope” (Rom 4:18). Rabbinic chronology calculates that Terah was still alive when Abraham left Haran — apparent contradiction with Acts 7:4, resolved variously in the harmonizing tradition.",
        "User original",
