        "Yahweh appeared to Abram",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>First patriarchal theophany.</strong> Genesis 12:7 is the first explicit “appearing” (<em>vayera</em>, <em>וַיֵּרָא</em>) of Yahweh to a patriarch — the verbal form becomes the rabbinic name for the Abraham theophany cycle (parashah <em>Vayera</em>). The pattern of revelation followed by altar-building structures the patriarchal narratives (12:7, 12:8, 13:18, 26:25, 35:7). Each altar marks a place of revelation, transforming geographic space into religious memory.",
        "User original",
