        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Ephrem the Syrian",
        "Ephrem the Syrian (360).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Ephrem the Syrian</strong> <em>Commentary on Genesis</em> <small>(c. 360 AD)</small><p>First theophany: &#x27;And the Lord appeared unto Abram&#x27;. Ephrem emphasises that the Word who appears here is the same Word who became flesh — the Father is invisible, but the Word makes Himself visible through theophanies. The altar Abram builds is the FIRST altar of true worship in the land that will become the holy land, prefiguring every later altar in the Mosaic-Aaronic priesthood and ultimately the Tewahedo tabot. Tewahedo eucharistic theology preserves Ephrem&#x27;s identification of the OT theophanies as appearances of the pre-incarnate Word.</p></aside>',
        "Ephrem the Syrian, Commentary on Genesis, Section XII.7. NPNF Series 2, vol. 13, ed. J. Gwynn / Schaff (1898). PD.",
