        "a tenth of all",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>The first tithe.</strong> Abraham’s tenth to Melchizedek is the first explicit tithe in Scripture, predating the Levitical tithe by centuries. Hebrews 7 develops this elaborately: Abraham’s tithing to Melchizedek demonstrates Melchizedek’s superiority to the Levitical priesthood (which is “in Abraham’s loins” when he tithes), thereby grounding Christ’s superior priestly order. The verse becomes central to early Christian arguments that Christ’s priesthood replaces, rather than continues, the Levitical line.",
        "User original",
