        "",
        "I have lifted up my hand to Yahweh",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>Oath of refusal.</strong> Abraham’s oath to the king of Sodom — refusing any spoils — uses the gesture of raising the hand, the standard Hebrew oath form (cf. Deut 32:40). The integration of “Yahweh” with “El Elyon” here as a single divine name signals Abraham’s identification of his God with the High God of Canaanite religion. The refusal of plunder is theologically loaded: Abraham will not be enriched by anyone but God, lest the nations claim credit for his prosperity. The verse models a piety that resists even legitimate gain when it might compromise covenant fidelity.",
