        6,
        "",
        "withheld you from sinning",
        "comm-reformation",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>Divine restraining grace.</strong> God claims to have actively prevented Abimelech from sinning — a striking case of preventive grace. The verse has been important for doctrines of common grace (Calvin, Kuyper) and divine providence, in which God restrains evil that would otherwise occur. The same pattern recurs in 1 Samuel 25 (David prevented from murdering Nabal by Abigail’s intercession). The theology has been controversial: it suggests divine action constraining human freedom in ways that challenge libertarian accounts of moral responsibility.",
        "User paraphrase; references Calvin",
