        "",
        "in the cave of the field of Machpelah",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>The first burial-place.</strong> Sarah’s burial establishes Israel’s first physical claim on the land of Canaan. The detail is theologically loaded: the patriarchs receive the land in promise; their burial places are the first concrete tenure. The motif persists — Joseph’s bones must be carried from Egypt (50:25) for burial in the land. Land-as-promise is never separated in the Hebrew Bible from land-as-burial-ground; the dead anchor the living to the place.",
