        "",
        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Ephrem the Syrian",
        "Ephrem the Syrian (360).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Ephrem the Syrian</strong> <em>Commentary on Genesis</em> <small>(c. 360 AD)</small><p>&#x27;And he dreamed, and behold a ladder set up on the earth, and the top of it reached to heaven: and behold the angels of God ascending and descending on it&#x27;. Ephrem reads the ladder as a Christ-Mary type: the ladder is Christ (Jn 1:51 — &#x27;angels of God ascending and descending upon the Son of man&#x27;), AND the ladder is Mary (because she bridges earth and heaven, bringing God to earth and lifting earth to God). Tewahedo Marian hymnody preserves the Jacob-ladder typology as one of Mary&#x27;s most prominent OT types, in the Wǝddase Maryam (Praise of Mary).</p></aside>',
        "Ephrem the Syrian, Commentary on Genesis, Section XXVIII.12. NPNF Series 2, vol. 13, ed. J. Gwynn / Schaff (1898). PD.",
