        "m",
        "",
        "word",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        '<strong>Yisra’el (<em>יִשְׂרָאֵל</em>).</strong> The patriarchal renaming. Two etymologies: (1) <em>sarah ‘im El</em> — "he strives with God," matching the angel’s explanation; (2) <em>El yisreh</em> — "God strives," or "God prevails." The very name of the people is built around a wrestling match with the divine — a foundational image of Israel’s relation to God: contention rather than easy submission.',
        "User original",
