        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>El-Bethel revisited.</strong> Jacob’s return to Bethel completes the inclusio begun at 28:12 — he left there with a vision of the heavenly stairway, returns with his household and ritually consecrates the site. The new altar-name <em>El-Bethel</em> (“God of the house of God”) joins divine name and place name, theologizing the geography. The pattern of return-to-altar-of-departure becomes a paradigm for biblical pilgrimage — the holy place is constituted not by intrinsic sacredness but by relationship of memory and revelation.",
