        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Ephrem the Syrian",
        "Ephrem the Syrian (360).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Ephrem the Syrian</strong> <em>Commentary on Genesis</em> <small>(c. 360 AD)</small><p>&#x27;And it came to pass... that Reuben went and lay with Bilhah his father&#x27;s concubine: and Israel heard it&#x27;. Ephrem reads Reuben&#x27;s sin as the COVENANT-RUPTURE moment that cost him the firstborn&#x27;s inheritance (cf. Gen 49:3-4, 1 Chr 5:1) — Reuben&#x27;s primogeniture passes to Joseph by way of the double-portion-to-his-two-sons. Tewahedo monastic-discipline tradition cites Reuben&#x27;s example: a single major moral failure can cost ecclesiastical office, even when individual salvation remains.</p></aside>',
