        "Amalek",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>Amalek.</strong> Amalek, here noted as the son of Eliphaz (Esau’s son) by his concubine Timna, becomes the eponym of Israel’s bitterest perpetual enemy. Exodus 17:8–16 describes Amalek’s unprovoked attack on Israel in the wilderness; Deuteronomy 25:17–19 commands Israel to “blot out the remembrance of Amalek”; 1 Samuel 15 records Saul’s failed extermination, costing him the kingdom; Esther’s villain Haman is identified as Agagite (Amalekite descendant). The genealogical note here makes Amalek’s enmity primordial — already encoded in the family tree before any historical encounter.",
        "User original",
