        "",
        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Ephrem the Syrian",
        "Ephrem the Syrian (360).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Ephrem the Syrian</strong> <em>Commentary on Genesis</em> <small>(c. 360 AD)</small><p>&#x27;And they... sold Joseph to the Ishmaelites for twenty pieces of silver&#x27;. Ephrem reads the twenty-pieces-of-silver sale as the OT type of Christ&#x27;s thirty-pieces-of-silver betrayal: same pattern (the righteous one sold by his own kin for silver-pieces), with the price escalating in the antitype. Tewahedo Holy-Week liturgy explicitly draws the Joseph-typology in the Wednesday-of-Holy-Week readings: Joseph sold prefigures Christ betrayed.</p></aside>',
        "Ephrem the Syrian, Commentary on Genesis, Section XXXVII.28. NPNF Series 2, vol. 13, ed. J. Gwynn / Schaff (1898). PD.",
