    (
        38,
        29,
        "",
        "Why have you made a breach",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>Perez — the breach.</strong> Perez’s name (<em>פֶּרֶץ</em>, “breach, breaking through”) etymologizes the unusual birth order — the second twin emerging first. The verb <em>paratz</em> (“to break through”) recurs as theological vocabulary throughout the Hebrew Bible, often connected to divine breakthroughs (cf. Mic 2:13). The naming becomes prophetic: Perez breaks through into firstborn position, his line becomes the Davidic-messianic line (Ruth 4:18–22; Matt 1:3). The “breaking through” motif is central — God’s chosen line breaks through expected birth-order conventions, just as Jacob over Esau, Joseph over Reuben, David over his elder brothers.",
        "User original",
    ),
