        "",
        "Pharaoh’s cup",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>The royal cup.</strong> The cup-bearer’s dream centers on Pharaoh’s cup — Egyptian royal court iconography is well-attested archaeologically, with cup-bearers (<em>wbꜣ</em>) holding intimate position near the king. The cup as royal symbol resonates throughout the Hebrew Bible — the cup of blessing (Ps 16:5), the cup of wrath (Isa 51:17), Jesus’s “cup” in Gethsemane (Mark 14:36). The cup-bearer’s restoration prefigures Joseph’s later cup-trick with his brothers (Gen 44:2) — Joseph plants his own cup as a structural inversion, the wronged man now becoming the one who manipulates cups.",
        "User original",
