        "",
        "God will shortly bring it to pass",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>The doubled dream.</strong> Joseph explicitly interprets the doubling of Pharaoh’s dreams as theological emphasis — when God doubles a dream, the matter is fixed and imminent. The pattern of doubling-as-divine-signal has wider biblical resonance: Pharaoh’s two dreams here, the two confirmations Gideon receives (Judg 6:36–40), Jesus’s Transfiguration witnessed by three disciples (Mark 9:2–10) doubling the cloud-voice motif of Sinai. Joseph’s hermeneutical principle — that dream-form encodes divine intention — establishes biblical dream-interpretation as systematic rather than ad hoc.",
        "User original",
