        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Ephrem the Syrian</strong> <em>Commentary on Genesis</em> <small>(c. 360 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Go unto Joseph; what he saith to you, do&#x27; (Pharaoh&#x27;s command to the famine-stricken people). Ephrem reads this verbatim as the Marian-Cana-prefiguration: &#x27;whatsoever he saith unto you, do it&#x27; (Jn 2:5 — Mary&#x27;s words to the servants at Cana). Tewahedo Marian theology preserves this typological pair: Joseph&#x27;s authoritative mediation in famine prefigures Mary&#x27;s authoritative mediation at Cana; both point to Christ as ultimate-provider.</p></aside>',
