        "God will surely visit you",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>God will visit you.</strong> Joseph’s death-bed prophecy — “God will surely visit you and bring you up out of this land” — echoes God’s promise to Jacob at 46:4 (“I will bring you up again”). The verb <em>paqod yifqod</em> (“surely visit”) is the same vocabulary used of Sarah’s miraculous conception (21:1, “Yahweh visited Sarah”) and becomes the standard Hebrew vocabulary for divine intervention. The phrase becomes Israel’s prophetic memory in Egypt — Exodus 3:16 has Moses say to the elders “Yahweh has surely visited you,” the language Joseph predicted. The verse establishes the Exodus framework before the Exodus events.",
