        "you shall carry up my bones",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>Joseph’s bones.</strong> Joseph extracts an oath from his brothers regarding his bones — paralleling Jacob’s burial oath. The oath is fulfilled at Exodus 13:19 (Moses takes Joseph’s bones at the Exodus) and Joshua 24:32 (Joshua buries them at Shechem). The bones become a mobile relic of covenant continuity — Israel literally carries Joseph through the wilderness and into the land. Hebrews 11:22 cites this verse as paradigmatic faith — Joseph’s confidence that the descent into Egypt was not the end of the story. The bones-vow theologizes the corpse: even in death, the patriarchs orient themselves toward the promised land.",
